{
  "name": "Doob",
  "isInstrument": true,
  "explanation": "Doob — a feature-for-feature model of the Moog Minimoog Model D, built from the original Operation Manual, the Technical Service Manual with its factory schematics, and the documented behaviour of the 2016 / 2022 reissues. Three band-limited oscillators (LO / 32' - 2', triangle / shark tooth / saw / square / wide and narrow pulse, reverse saw on oscillator 3, ±7 st detune, oscillator 3 detachable from the keyboard), a five-source mixer that overloads into the 4-pole 24 dB Moog ladder (self-oscillating at EMPHASIS 10, regeneration from 7.5, keyboard control 1/3 and 2/3), two RC contour generators (attack / decay / sustain, DECAY switch, 10 µF timing, 10 s / 30 s ranges), noise generator (white / pink / red), modulation mix (oscillator 3 or noise through the audio-taper MOD wheel to pitch and / or filter), sample-and-hold keyboard with low-note priority, single-trigger legato and glide, A-440 reference, external-input preamp with overload lamp, and the reissue extras (LFO, filter-contour modulation source, key priority, multi-trigger, scales, bend range). 57 controls: all knobs and wheels are real DAW parameters; switches and settings are packed into the remaining host slots.",
